From: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm: default THP defrag to defer+madvise instead of madvise

The unconditional default-flags initializer always sets
TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_DEFRAG_REQ_MADV_FLAG ("madvise" defrag mode),
regardless of the CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_ALWAYS/MADVISE Kconfig
choice that controls *whether* THP is used. "madvise" defrag mode runs
synchronous compaction in the page-fault path for MADV_HUGEPAGE-tagged
VMAs — fine under transparent_hugepage=madvise, but this workstation's
ai-only preset switches to transparent_hugepage=always (CUDA pinned
host buffers, GreenBoost T2 staging), so every anonymous fault becomes
THP-eligible and can hit synchronous compaction stalls under memory
pressure from concurrent inference + gaming + VMs.

"defer+madvise" keeps the same allocation behavior but pushes
compaction to khugepaged/kswapd in the background instead of stalling
the faulting thread — the standard recommendation for desktops/servers
running transparent_hugepage=always (matches guidance long given for
Redis/MongoDB-style THP=always workloads). Runtime-overridable via
`echo defer+madvise > /sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/defrag`; this
patch only changes the compiled-in default.

Forward-Port-Notes: mm/huge_memory.c (transparent_hugepage_flags initializer)
Signed-off-by: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@pm.me>
---
 mm/huge_memory.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/huge_memory.c b/mm/huge_memory.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/mm/huge_memory.c
+++ b/mm/huge_memory.c
@@ -63,6 +63,6 @@ unsigned long transparent_hugepage_flags __read_mostly =
 #ifdef CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE
 	(1<<TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_REQ_MADV_FLAG)|
 #endif
-	(1<<TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_DEFRAG_REQ_MADV_FLAG)|
+	(1<<TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_DEFRAG_KSWAPD_OR_MADV_FLAG)|
 	(1<<TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_DEFRAG_KHUGEPAGED_FLAG)|
 	(1<<TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_USE_ZERO_PAGE_FLAG);
